# Keep the build context small and -- more importantly -- keep the host's own
# out-of-container CMake build tree out of the image entirely. If build/ were
# copied in, its CMakeCache.txt (host absolute paths, host generator choice)
# would corrupt the in-container `cmake -S . -B build` configure step.
build/
build-*/
cmake-build-*/

.git/
.github/

# Large / irrelevant to the C++ build; just bloats the context upload. Kept
# to genuinely inert files only (never referenced by any CMakeLists.txt rule):
# snapshot.bin and the *.log files are plain data/output, not build inputs.
*.log
snapshot.bin
violations_vps_*.log

# Editor/IDE and OS cruft.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Deliberately NOT excluding branding/, *.md, docs/, apps/finalis-wallet,
# apps/finalis-explorer, sdk/, services/, fuzz/, etc. even though
# finalis-node/finalis-cli don't need them at runtime: CMakeLists.txt
# references branding/*.png and several *.md files in an install(FILES ...)
# rule, and calls add_executable() on other app dirs unconditionally (not
# gated behind FINALIS_BUILD_FUZZ/Qt5Widgets_FOUND). We never run
# `cmake --install` here so that rule shouldn't matter in practice, but after
# the build/ context bug, it's not worth risking a second one to save a few
# KB of context upload.
